This project does all three. The text is treated as read-only data: it is
verified on download (6236 ayat, correct count per surah) and is never
edited by application code.

Warsh riwayah (عن نافع، من طريق الأصبهاني)
------------------------------------------

For readers who follow the Warsh riwayah, the Quran text plus the Madani page
(604) and juz (30) boundaries come from the King Fahd Complex (KFGQPC) Warsh
Uthmanic data, the authoritative publisher of the Warsh Madani Mushaf. It is
downloaded with `pnpm data:fetch:warsh` (from the verbatim KFGQPC mirror at
https://github.com/thetruetruth/quran-data-kfgqpc) and stored, unchanged, at:

    prisma/data/quran-warsh-asbahani.json

The per-ayah page and juz are taken from, and every ayah is cross-checked
against, the independent quran-meta library (https://github.com/quran-center/quran-meta,
MIT), which exposes the Warsh Madani page/juz/count metadata. Nothing is written
unless every check passes: 6214 ayat (the Madani count), the correct Madani count
per surah, every ayah's page/juz agreeing with quran-meta, full 604-page and
30-juz coverage, and the Madani markers (Al-Baqarah is 285 ayat, not Hafs's 286).
The Warsh text and its numbers are read-only data, never edited by application
code. KFGQPC content remains the property of the King Fahd Complex; it is used
here, unmodified, for the non-commercial educational purpose of helping people
read and revise the Quran.

